summary:
One Contents panel replaces the two navigation copies. The panel is `div#contents-panel` with the classes `offcanvas-lg offcanvas-start sticky-lg-top`. Under lg (992 px) it is a fixed drawer that slides in under the sticky header. From lg it stays the sticky 25 % sidebar it is today.

A `Contents` link opens the drawer. It is an `a.btn` element with `href="#contents"`, `aria-controls="contents-panel"` and `aria-expanded`, placed last among the header controls and hidden from lg. Because it is a link, the header keeps exactly five `button` elements. Under lg the Tab order reads skip link, the five buttons, `Contents`, then `Containers` when the drawer is open; at 1280 it is unchanged.

`Showcase.ts` toggles the registry class `show` itself, with no engine. Five routes fold the drawer at once: activating a link in it, Escape (focus returns to the `Contents` link), focus moving out of it, a click outside it, and the viewport reaching lg.

One IntersectionObserver marks the current section's link with `aria-current="location"`, `fw-semibold` and a full underline. The current section is the last one, in page order, that intersects the viewport's top quarter. When that link is out of view, the observer callback scrolls the panel (never the document) to show it. There is no back-to-contents control, because the header link under lg and the sticky sidebar from lg are always one step away.

At 390 px the page opens on the first group heading after the body container's `py-5` padding. Today it opens after the always-open index, which measured 342 × 1,631 px in the 2026-10-03 light-390 capture.

What stays unchanged:
- the main column's width, because `row g-5` becomes `row gx-5` with identical horizontal gutters;
- the five header buttons;
- the `.sticky-lg-top` inline-style contract;
- all 72 sections in `main > div`;
- the class-token census;
- the `@app/browser` export list.

The unit:
- rewrites the factories.test.ts:805-867 literals;
- adds `openContents` and `clickContents` helpers and routes all seven Contents clicks in setupBrowser.ts through them (the scout named four);
- adds an open step to J1, J2, J3 and the variant case;
- adds the `contents-drawer` capture state, two Showcase cases and one setup case;
- updates the guide's § Showcase.

After the gates pass, rebuild `showcase/browser.html` with `npm run build` and `npm run build:showcase`, and check that a second build hashes equal. Commit the page with the unit and fast-forward origin/main by refspec. Estimate: 9 lane-hours.

isolation:
The shell isolates each section as a destination, not as a separate view, because all 72 sections stay in one document:
- Each section is a region named by its `h3`.
- A Contents link lands that heading 8 px under the header through the root's `scroll-padding-top`.
- At 390 the drawer folds at once, so the landed section fills the screen.
- The current-section marker shows the reader's position in the sidebar or the drawer.

No section, group block or `main > div` child changes. `collectBootstrapGroups`, J3's region readings, the census, the partition, preservation and every `COMPONENT_TABLES` row therefore read the same population and specimens.

**Room for stage B:** `createContents` and the observer are driven by `GROUPS` and `SECTIONS`. A group such as `{ id: 'native', title: 'Native surfaces' }` placed between `interactions` and `tailwindcss` (constants.ts:76-86) adds one uppercase label and its links to the drawer and sidebar with no shell change. Then:
- J1's `TAILWIND Tailwind on Bootstrap markup` reading still holds;
- J3 and the variant case pick up the group's sections from the constants;
- the group's engine-leaf specimens get their own tables beside the existing ones, which stay as they are.

The drawer cannot collide with a stage B leaf:
- it is not `.offcanvas`;
- it has no `data-bs-*` attribute and no `aria-modal`, so B3's offcanvas changes and the responsive resize hide never select it;
- it lives outside main;
- a native top-layer dialog or a promoted float paints over it.

