isolation:
**1. Section frame without width cost.** `createSection` (factories.ts:555-574) wraps the title in a heading row: `div.d-flex.flex-wrap.align-items-baseline.justify-content-between.column-gap-3.row-gap-1.pb-2.mb-2.border-bottom`. The row holds `h3#ID-title.h5.mb-0`, with its text and id unchanged, and an anchor chip, `code.text-body-secondary.user-select-all[aria-hidden="true"]`, reading `#ID`.
- The chip is text and never a link. It adds no tab stop and no second link named by a title; J3 resolves each title as one rendered link (integration.test.ts:437).
- The lead stays a direct `p.text-body-secondary.mb-4` child, so `collectContrastSubjects` keeps its `:scope > p` selector.
- The engine hint and the engine table stay at child indices 2 and 3.
- The section keeps `section#ID.mb-5[aria-labelledby]` and gets no horizontal padding. The figure grid, the `ratio-4x3` Live examples frame (live-components.html:7) that drives the scrollspy rows, and every matrix keep their widths.

**2. Chapter frame.** Each `h2#group-ID` trades `pb-2 border-bottom` for `pt-2 border-top border-primary` and keeps `h3 mb-4`, with `mt-5` on every group but the first (factories.ts:820-826). A group opens with a primary rule above its title. A section opens with a neutral rule under its title.

**3. Specimen frame.** The figure, column, and card-body shapes stay: `card flex-fill mb-0` inside `col d-flex` or `col-xl-12 d-flex`, with `card-body` and a `figcaption.card-footer.bg-transparent.small` whose first child is the title span.

**4. Paint isolation.** By CSS stacking rules, these specimens sit in the root stacking context with no stacking context between them and the root:
- frozen tooltips (tooltips.html:57, z-index 1080);
- frozen popovers (popovers.html:50, 1070);
- the sticky log (position-helpers.html:43, 1020);
- the z-index stage's `z-3` panel (z-index.html:7);
- active and focused page links (3);
- focused accordion buttons (3);
- validation input-group states and tooltips (3 to 5).

They tie or out-stack the header's z-index 3, so they paint over the header when scrolled beneath it; the values come from dist/src/bootstrap/index.css. The fix extends the existing `z-0` stage convention. `z-0` goes on the card body of 23 figures that hold no live dropdown, modal, or offcanvas:
- accordion.html:4, :96, :144;
- pagination.html:5, :32, :65, :94;
- input-group.html:8, :81, :117, :154;
- validation.html:8, :40, :73, :109;
- popovers.html:48, :73, :96, :119, :142;
- tooltips.html:53;
- position-helpers.html:40;
- z-index.html:4.

A card body is a flex item of `.card`, so `z-0` alone makes it a stacking context, and specimen geometry doesn't change. I refuse a stacking context per section or per figure: a live modal inside it would paint under the body-level backdrop, and an open dropdown would paint under the next figure. An added hit-order case proves the result, and removing one `z-0` is its control.

**5. Native slot.** A Native group, `{ id: 'native', title: 'Native' }`, goes after `tailwindcss` in `GROUPS` (constants.ts:76-86). It lands with the first stage B unit that ships a demo, never earlier. An empty group renders nothing (factories.ts:665, :819), but the variant case would expect its `group-native` heading.
- **Sections.** Each section (`native-dialog`, `native-collapse`, `native-floats`) is a fragment, `sections/native-ID.html`, built as a pair row: `div.row.row-cols-1.row-cols-xl-2.g-4`.
- **Figures.** A `Default` figure, `#native-ID-default`, carries the Bootstrap markup. An `Opt-in` figure, `#native-ID-leaf`, carries the engine leaf. Both are `figure.card.flex-fill.mb-0` inside `col d-flex`.
- **Status chips.** Each caption keeps its title span first and adds a status chip after it: `span.badge.rounded-pill.text-bg-secondary` reading `Default` (white on #6c757d, 4.69:1), or `span.badge.rounded-pill.text-primary-emphasis.bg-primary-subtle` reading `Opt-in`.
- **Tables.** Opener names carry the variant (`Open the default dialog`, `Open the native dialog`), so no row of the 18 `COMPONENT_TABLES` resolves them. Their own tables append.
- **Existing readers.** Placing the group after Tailwind keeps `collectBootstrapGroups`, the existing sections' order, and every existing table unchanged. In that landing unit, the census exempts the Native group as it exempts `interactions` (sections/integration.test.ts:25, :114), and the variant expectation stops at the Tailwind group.
- **Top layer.** A native dialog or a promoted popover renders in the top layer, so the `z-0` card bodies never trap a leaf demo.

test_cochanges.change:
Retitle the case to 'lands first and deep contents headings below the sticky chrome after a viewport resize'. At 390 px:
- follow links through `followContents`;
- wait for `scrollPaddingTop` to equal the header height plus the summary height plus 8;
- read each heading 8 px under the summary's bottom.
The 1280 `.sticky-lg-top` flush assertions (:739-746) and the removed-offset control stay.

At 390 and 768 px, under the three faces, in both color modes, the case reads:
- arrival: a collapsed `Contents` disclosure and zero rendered navs;
- the summary's box, position, top, and z-index equal under `bootstrap` and `unexcluded`, with every `tailwindcss` departure attributed through `attributeChromeToken`;
- the bar's top equal to the header's bottom after a scroll;
- after `clickDisclosure`, one rendered nav and scrollWidth at or under clientWidth;
- a followed link closes the drawer and lands its heading 8 px under the bar, and the next Tab lands inside the target section;
- Escape closes the drawer and focuses the summary;
- summary contrast of 4.5:1 or more.
Control: removing `position-sticky` breaks the bar-top reading.

At 390:
- the summary is rendered and `collapsed`;
- `resolveRendered('link', 'Containers')` throws (the folded control);
- `clickDisclosure('Contents')` opens it, leaving one rendered nav with 72 reachable links;
- `{Enter}` on the focused summary folds it;
- the summary's contrast reads 4.5:1 or more under three faces × two color modes, with the `buildContrast(4.5)` control.

At 1280:
- the summary is not rendered and is no tab stop;
- the sticky nav renders 72 reachable links;
- planting `open` on the `details` element still renders no second nav (the control).

